  "notes": "CONJUGATION (godan-u):\n- Negative: {纏|まと}わない\n- Te-form: {纏|まと}って\n- Past: {纏|まと}った\n- Potential: {纏|まと}える\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive. Takes を for the garment or quality being worn.\n\nWRITING:\nOften written in hiragana as まとう due to the complexity of the kanji {纏|まと}.\n\nUSAGE:\nA literary, elegant word for wearing or being draped in something. Unlike {着|き}る (the everyday word for wearing), {纏|まと}う evokes a sense of being enveloped or wrapped. It is frequently used figuratively for intangible qualities like an atmosphere, aura, or mystery.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {衣|ころも}を{纏|まと}う: to be clad in robes\n- {雰囲気|ふんいき}を{纏|まと}う: to carry an atmosphere\n- {霧|きり}を{纏|まと}う: to be shrouded in mist\n- {鎧|よろい}を{纏|まと}う: to wear armor",
